From 46b4cc918a5b577f7d188f89de3421e9aae64689 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alia Holes <thealiaholes@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:12:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] tests: drive the SMS plugin against a fake device

Load the real kdeconnect_sms plugin with a TestDevice that records every
packet sent, and check that it asks for conversations when the link comes up
and again after a reconnect, sends a light request_conversation on the
heartbeat, reports the sync times on its D-Bus adaptor, reports an unreadable
attachment instead of sending, and shrinks a 4 MB photo under the image
budget before it goes out; that a send from a worker thread still goes out;
and that a silent phone raises the stall notification once per episode,
holds the warning state through many heartbeats, and clears it on a reply;
that a link flapping faster than the window still raises it; that a device
whose every send fails raises it; and that a disconnect really closes it
(seen through a stand-in org.freedesktop.Notifications on the test's session
bus) and a reconnect decides afresh.

smssyncstatustest drives SmsSyncKeeper with a fake clock through many
unanswered heartbeats and checks what the SMS app would show at every
15-second step: never blank, the warning continuous once the window has
passed, and the first unanswered request never moved; also reconnects every
60 s with no replies (warns, clock never reset), a phone away for an hour
(gets its window back), a debounced link-up (never "answered" from an older
reply, its request deferred, not dropped) and every send failing.
smspastetest checks the asynchronous, per-user paste of a bitmap, the text
fallbacks, and that a failed save is reported with its reason.
